.TH ARATECONF 1 "November 2025" "fftrate 1.6.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
arateconf \- interactive ALSA configuration tool for fftrate
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B arateconf
is an interactive, self-explanatory utility to create ALSA configuration
files (~/.asoundrc), using
.B fftrate
as the rate-conversion plugin.
.P
By default it is configured for HiRes 32-bit Integer 192kHz. The objective
is to bypass the low-quality built-in hardware resamplers found in Intel
HDA/Realtek codecs by forcing ALSA to always talk to the hardware at a
fixed 192kHz/32-bit rate, letting fftrate handle all real-time sample-rate
conversion in userspace.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage message.
.TP
.B \-\-help\-all
Show all help information.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version information.
.SH USAGE
Run
.B arateconf
with no arguments to enter interactive mode:
.RS
.nf
$ arateconf
.fi
.RE
.P
For an Intel HDA codec on the motherboard, try 32-bit/192000Hz. For USB
headsets/DACs, try 16-bit/48000Hz.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B 0, 1, ...
Select a sound card from the list.
.TP
.B U
Toggle "used" flag for the current device.
.TP
.B P / R
Set current device as default player / recorder.
.TP
.B O / I
Set output / input hardware device.
.TP
.B F
Change sample format (rate, bit depth, channels).
.TP
.B C
Select converter plugin (fftrate, speexrate, samplerate, ...).
.TP
.B A / M
Show / edit plugin chain (Convert, Expand, Asym, Dmix, Dsnoop, etc).
.TP
.B T
Run hardware compatibility test on all configured devices.
.TP
.B S
Save configuration to ~/.asoundrc.
.TP
.B X
Delete existing ~/.asoundrc.
.TP
.B ESC
Exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Configure an Intel HDA output/input at HiRes 32-bit/192kHz, run hardware test, then save:
.RS
.nf
$ arateconf
   (press 0 to select "HDA-Intel - HDA Intel PCH")
   (press F, set Format: 192000 Hz, 2 ch, 'S32_LE')
   (press T to test)

Testing H/W compatibility ...

Device: PCH
Output:
 Open device "hw:PCH,0" ... Ok.
 Set rate 192000 Hz ... Ok.
 Set channels 2 ... Ok.
 Set format \(aqS32_LE\(aq ... Ok.
 Set buffer size 30720 \-> 30720
 Set period size 7680 \-> 7680
Input:
 Open device "hw:PCH,0" ... Ok.
 Set rate 192000 Hz ... Ok.
 Set format \(aqS32_LE\(aq ... Ok.
 Set buffer size 30720 \-> 30720
 Set period size 7680 \-> 7680

   (press S to save to ~/.asoundrc)
.fi
.RE
.TP
Verify the resulting config by playing/recording at a lower native rate
(fftrate transparently up/down-converts to/from the fixed 192kHz hardware rate):
.RS
.nf
$ aplay audio_test_48kHz_16bit.wav
Input:  48000 Hz, 2 ch, \(aqs16_le\(aq (0x2): dummy = 0, period = 1920
Output: 192000 Hz, 2 ch, \(aqs32_le\(aq (0xa): dummy = 0, period = 7680
Rates:  48000 \-\-> 192000 (J: 0.00%, T: FFT, W: Vorbis)
Ok.
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.I ~/.asoundrc
\- generated ALSA configuration (or
.I /etc/asound.conf
when run as root).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pcm_conv (1),
.BR asoundrc (5)
